        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "34cc3993-d781-5465-a73b-e23f61edb1e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Republican Party, GOP\n- Laws: Kansas–Nebraska Act, Missouri Compromise\n- People: Stephen A. Douglas, Franklin Pierce\n- Places: Kansas, Nebraska, Illinois\n- Concepts: popular sovereignty, slavery in the territories\n\nFacts:\n- The Republican Party, also called the GOP for \"Grand Old Party,\" is one of the world's oldest extant political parties.\n- The Republican Party emerged in 1854 to oppose the Kansas–Nebraska Act.\n- The Kansas–Nebraska Act dissolved the terms of the Missouri Compromise and allowed slave or free status in the territories to be decided by popular sovereignty.\n- The Kansas–Nebraska Act created the territories of Kansas and Nebraska.\n- Democratic Senator Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois and President Franklin Pierce drafted the Kansas–Nebraska Act.",
